WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.447
Real machine learning projects rarely begin with a small Data frame typed directly into Python.

00:00:06.447 --> 00:00:14.552
Data may come from CSV or TSV files, Excel workbooks, APIs that return JSON, or databases queried with SQL.

00:00:14.552 --> 00:00:20.356
The technical loading step is only part of the problem.

00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:23.752
You also need to understand data provenance.

00:00:23.752 --> 00:00:27.492
Who produced the data? What does each field mean?

00:00:27.492 --> 00:00:29.532
When was the data collected?

00:00:29.532 --> 00:00:31.392
How often is it updated?

00:00:31.392 --> 00:00:34.182
Are you allowed to use it for this purpose?

00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:40.527
Those questions are especially important in machine learning because a model can learn patterns that reflect the

00:00:40.527 --> 00:00:44.047
limitations or biases of the source data.

00:00:44.047 --> 00:00:50.966
External data must still go through the same quality and interpretation checks you learned earlier in the course.
